            <ArticleTitle>Aortic dissection following heart transplantation.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>156-158</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <ELocationID EIdType="doi" ValidYN="Y">10.1111/jocs.13096</ELocationID>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>A 75-year-old male with a previous orthotopic heart transplantation performed 28 years ago was incidentally discovered to have an asymptomatic chronic type A aortic dissection. Catheter-induced dissection during coronary angiography was believed to be the culprit factor. Aortic root replacement and aortic valve reconstruction were successfully performed.</AbstractText>
